&nbsp;

Be careful! The world of creating custom inserts for your game boxes is addictive! You will soon find yourself making random boxes for random objects in random containers! xD

&nbsp;

In all seriousness however, it is very easy. You need:

&nbsp;

A good, sharp exacto knife with extra blades

A -METAL- ruler (plastic or wood will shave and cause uneven lines)

White glue (elmers is great)

Foamcore. (I like black, white is fine. Personal preference)<br />&nbsp;

Not necessary, but very nice: A self healing cutting mat. If you don&#39;t want to drop the cash for that, some big sheets of cardboard work just as well.

&nbsp;

All of the above is available at your local craft store most likely. Jo-ann, Michaels, Hobby Lobby if you are in the States all work great. If not, I am certain you know what your local variety of bigbox craft store is and with a proper list the people there can help you find it. The Plano boxes are almost always found at those stores too (people use them to store beads and jewelery parts) but if that doesn&#39;t work you can also find them often at fishing supply stores.

&nbsp;

For making:

First, watch this video:&nbsp;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3hfKaDX2P2k&amp;index=30&amp;list=UUzm-X8tDtEyrOeYiC9SdcJg

(edit, if the edit is working, here is the playlist for all 3 foamcore videos:&nbsp;https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PL3qhmvdVjd2uRvjS_6G3tcH1bGK6vHz2R )

(and others on their channel) - they do an excellent job of explaining what to do.

Next: &nbsp;be patient! It takes a lot of patience, otherwise you&#39;ll rip the foamcore and cause uneven edges, or you&#39;ll cut things the wrong size. Measure multiple times and think about it, them measure again.&nbsp;

But it is a lot of fun and feels really good.&nbsp;
